==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr}} {{term|ballet|lang=fr}}, from {{etyl|it}} {{term|balletto||short dance, ballet|lang=it}}, diminutive form of {{term|ballo||ball|lang=it}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}}  {{IPA|/ˈbæl.eɪ/}}, {{SAMPA|/"b{l.eI/}}
* {{rhymes|æleɪ}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[classical]] form of [[dance]].
# A [[theatrical]] [[presentation]] of such [[dancing]], usually with [[music]], sometimes in the form of a [[story]].
# A [[company]] or [[school]] that practices the very art of ballet.

====Derived terms====
* [[ballet dancer]]
* [[ballet flats]]
* [[ballet music]]

